            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/1938640014560165</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="UNLABELLED">Synovial chondromatosis is a rare pathology in the foot and ankle region. We present a case of concomitant tenosynovial chondromatosis of the extensor digitorum longus tendon and synovial chondromatosis of the ankle, which was successfully treated by extensor digitorum tendon tendoscopy and ankle arthroscopy.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="LEVELS OF EVIDENCE" NlmCategory="METHODS">Therapeutic, Level IV: Case study.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2014 The Author(s).</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
